# riscv32 without atomics: rv32i on QEMU's `virt` machine, on an `rv32` hart with the A
# extension switched off (and M and C with it), so the hardware refuses an atomic,
# multiply, divide or compressed instruction. QEMU's own `rv32i` model has no Zicsr, which
# a machine-mode kernel needs, so it cannot be used. The roadmap's Phase 4 exit and
# docs/portability.md's oldest claim — that code needing a capability the target lacks
# is absent rather than stubbed — are what this preset tests.
#
# Everything `riscv32-virt` runs, minus what compare-and-swap buys: the kernel takes the
# uniprocessor lock family throughout.
ARCH_RISCV32=y
RISCV32_NO_ATOMICS=y
EARLY_CONSOLE=y
DEBUG_BUILD=y
QEMU_EXIT=y
SIZE_BUDGET_KIB=560
